condition_name: Deep Vein Thrombosis
condition_slug: deep-vein-thrombosis
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "Formation of blood clot(s) in the deep veins of the calf muscles or pelvis. It has the potential of being dislodged to the lungs, causing pulmonary embolism"
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical Features
    features[2]: Could be asymptomatic,Pain and swelling of the leg (calf muscles)
investigations[7]: FBC and differentials,Prothrombin time,KCCT,Venous doppler of the leg/pelvic vessels,Echocardiography,Electrocardiography,Venography (pelvic or calf veins)
treatment:
  goals[3]: Lyse the clot,Prevent clot from being dislodged,Relieve inflammation
  non_drug[1]: "Avoid stasis, by encouraging ambulation and some degree of physical activity"
  drug[2]: "Heparin 5000 - 10,000 units by intravenous injection followed by subcutaneous injection of 15,000 units every 12 hours or intravenous infusion at 15 - 25 units/kg/hr, with close laboratory monitoring. Aim to achieve APTT of 1.5 to 2.5 of control.",Warfarin 1 - 5 mg orally daily for 6 - 12 weeks. Maintain Target INR at 2 – 2.5
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[2]: "Bleeding from heparin, warfarin",Osteoporosis (heparin)
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[3]: Cellulitis,Infarctive crisis in sicklers,Abscess (pyomyositis)
complications[1]: Pulmonary embolism
prevention[2]: Low molecular weight heparin 5000 units subcutaneously every 12 hours,Early mobilization
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null